  "configuration_id": "config_040",
  "reason": "Evidence: The strongest results (0.7062–0.7150) all use scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool, with concat fusion outperforming weighted by ~0.9%. The RNA encoder is the largest untested dimension—scgpt has never been evaluated. This experiment tests whether scgpt, paired with the proven-best image encoder (ViT-L), aggregation (avgpool), and fusion (concat), can surpass the current best (config_042, 0.7150). It is the best next step because it isolates the single most impactful unexplored variable while holding all other components at their empirically validated settings, reducing confounds. If scgpt matches or beats scvi_n200, the remaining 3 experiments can exploit that finding (e.g., testing transformer aggregation or singleprofile variants around scgpt). Expected relative cost: comparable to config_042 (~4.5 GPU hours), since it shares the same image encoder, aggregation, and fusion strategy; scgpt training cost should be in the same range as scvi_n200."
}

